    (kind note)
    (seq 159)
    (text
     "steer/testparse.rkt: parse-test-output(cmd, output) detects pytest/dotnet/rackunit from the command or the output's own signature, returns failures (id file line message) in report order + a one-line summary. checks.rkt now keeps up to 1MiB of output (was a 64KiB tail only), so a long dotnet run's first failures are not lost. check-findings in cmd-tasks.rkt shows the summary in the headline plus up to 3 test-failed findings, --full/--limit lift the cap, unrecognised output falls back to the old raw tail unchanged. Fixtures are sanitized REAL runs (pytest 9.1, dotnet 10 xunit on a broken GuardClauses copy, raco test), not synthesized: tests/fixtures/test-output/. Verified end to end through steer done.")
